<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daimyo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The daimyo were the great feudal lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> who ruled domains and commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> retainers. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> about 260 daimyo governed their domains semi-autonomously, subject to shogunal regulation and the system of alternate attendance in Edo. The daimyo domains were abolished in 1871 after the Meiji Restoration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daimyo.jpg" alt="Daimyo" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Japan_Genki1-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
